# Ticket 4 — Suspicious Email

## Issue
User reported receiving a suspicious email and contacted IT for assistance.

## User Impact
The user was concerned that the email could be a phishing or fraudulent message.

## Troubleshooting Performed

Asked the user who sent the email.
Reviewed the sender information.
Inspected the full email header details.
Determined whether the message contained suspicious indicators.
Confirmed whether the user clicked any links.
Confirmed whether the user entered credentials or other information.
Advised the user not to interact with suspicious links or attachments.
Marked/reported the message as spam or fraud.

## Findings

The email was identified as suspicious and potentially fraudulent.

The user confirmed that they had not entered any credentials or sensitive information.

## Resolution

The suspicious email was reported as spam/fraud and the user was advised not to interact with similar messages.

## Ticket Status
**Resolved**

## Skills Demonstrated

Phishing identification
Email security
Security awareness
Email header analysis
Incident triage
User communication
Security incident documentation


